# Desktop Twin · UI language file (English)
#
# 481 entries · for Desktop Twin 0.2.4 · see Localization/README.md
#
# How to use: rename this file to DesktopTwin.lng and put it next to
# DesktopTwin.exe (same base name as the executable). There is no language
# switch inside the app — the presence of that file is what selects the language.
# To get the built-in Simplified Chinese back, just remove or rename the file.
#
# Keys must not be changed; translate only the text after '='.
# Keep {0} / {1} placeholders (their order may change).
# Use \n for a line break, \t for a tab. Missing or empty keys fall back to
# the built-in Simplified Chinese. Debug logs stay in Chinese on purpose,
# because that is what support asks you to send when something breaks.


