Startup.AutoLaunchSkipped.Title=Auto-launch skipped
Startup.AutoLaunchSkipped.Message=Auto-launch was skipped: the target program needs administrator rights but that has not been confirmed yet, or this system (UAC off) cannot really drop privileges.\nIf it is the first case: check both "Launch automatically after connecting" and "Run the target program as administrator", confirm once, and it will run as administrator from then on. You can also launch it manually from Control Center → Launch in the twin now.
